/-- **`lem:geometry`** (Dyadic facts and boundary packing).

Intersecting boxes are nested.  A box has `2^A` children, which partition it,
and the leaves of a finite convex tree partition its root.

This is the count of children. -/
theorem lem_geometry_card_boxChildren (α : Anisotropy) (q : AnisoBox α) :
    (boxChildren α q).card = 2 ^ α.homogeneousDimension :=
  card_boxChildren α q

/-- **`lem:geometry`** (Dyadic facts and boundary packing).

The leaves of a finite convex tree partition its root; all these sets are
measurable.

This is the resulting additivity of the measure. -/
theorem lem_geometry_volume_root_eq_sum_volume_leaves
    {α : Anisotropy} (T : FiniteConvexTree α) :
    volume (boxSet α T.root) = ∑ l ∈ treeLeaves T, volume (boxSet α l) :=
  volume_root_eq_sum_volume_leaves T

/-- **`lem:size`** (Size comparison and zero size).

There is `C_{α,s}` such that
`M_{T,s}(f) ≤ sup_{(p,t) ∈ closure Ω_T} (|f|^s * Θ_t(p))^{1/s}
